# Auto-publish to GitHub (required after tasks)

When you **finish any task** that changed tracked project files in `blofin-auto-trader`, **commit and push** to `origin/main` unless the user explicitly says "do not push this session."

## Git safety protocol

- NEVER update git config
- NEVER run destructive git commands (push --force, hard reset) unless explicitly requested
- NEVER skip hooks (--no-verify) unless explicitly requested
- NEVER force-push to main/master
- Avoid `git commit --amend` unless all amend conditions in user rules are met
- NEVER commit `.env`, credentials, `state/`, `logs/`, `__pycache__/`, `*.gguf`, `dashboard/node_modules/`, or other gitignored secrets

## After every task with code changes

1. Run `git status` and `git diff` in parallel with `git log -3 --oneline`
2. Stage relevant tracked/untracked **code** files only (`git add` specific paths or `git add -A` then verify status)
3. Draft a concise commit message focused on **why**
4. Commit and **push** to `origin main`:
   ```powershell
   git push origin main
   ```
5. Run `git status` after push to confirm clean or report what's left

## When to skip

- Question-only / review-only tasks with **zero** file changes
- User explicitly says not to commit or push this session
- Push fails (auth/network) — report error; leave local commit if commit succeeded

## Scope

Applies to **all** tasks in this repo: features, fixes, scripts, dashboard, Cursor skills/rules, docs. One task may be one commit or a few logical commits; always end with push when possible.
